# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed (this workspace produces binaries).

# The wasm-bindgen build output (`scripts/web-build.sh`) — regenerated
# from the browser renderer and editor on every build, and the .wasm
# alone can run tens of MB.
/web/dist/

# --- Blizzard-owned content: NEVER commit ---
# The user's legally-installed 1.12.1 client. Read at runtime; not redistributed.
/WoW
# Cached / extracted assets derived from the user's install.
/extracted/
/out/
# Real client files used as test fixtures (document expected paths, do not commit).
**/tests/fixtures/

# --- benilla's own local state ---
# The one folder benilla persists into: config.toml, macros/, bindings/, saved-variables.lua,
# camera/. A dev build resolves it to the main checkout (so linked worktrees share one, bar a
# worktree with a .probe-identity, which keeps its own); a release build puts it beside the
# binary — which is why it is not called `benilla/`: that name collides with the binary of the
# same name. Machine-local by definition — `crate::local_state`
# is the only thing in the tree that may write it.
/benilla-config

# The account a scripted run from this checkout logs in as (scripts/probe-identity.sh and the
# client's account guard read it): WOW_USER=, WOW_PASS=, WOW_CHAR=, one per line. A credential.
/.probe-identity

# Profiling output: `--features bevy/trace_chrome` drops a multi-GB flame chart in the cwd, which
# otherwise leaves the checkout "dirty".
trace-*.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
/.idea/
# Claude Code: settings and skills under .claude/ are each person's own.
/.claude/

# Python bytecode from the `scripts/` tooling.
__pycache__/

# The vanilla addon corpus the UI engine's real-addon tests read (third-party content): a symlink
# beside `WoW`, or `BENILLA_ADDON_CORPUS`.
/wow-addons-vanilla

# The C sysroot for the wasm Lua build — fetched by scripts/web-setup.sh, ~300 MB
/tools/wasi-sdk/
/tools/binaryen/

# Pull Fiction editor dependencies and locally extracted game UI assets.
/web/editor/node_modules/
/web/editor/.vite/

# Local agent work, replay caches, logs, and API credentials.
/.agent/
/.agents/
/.codex/
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
# Historical machine-specific investigation notes stay local.
/docs/PERFORMANCE-REVIEW-2026-09-10.md

# Local environment configuration and credentials. Keep documented templates only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample

# Generated Python/editor tooling caches.
.pytest_cache/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Optional project-local Python development environment.
/.venv/
